Well, I suffered one of the dumbest deaths I've ever seen.
Spoilers may follow.

I was playing a dopey elf, and, by luck, I found a polished silver shield and
a wand of polymorph early on.  I polypiled on a altar and offered until I
got a Sunsword and Mjollnir (which soon became rustproofed +8 Sunsword and
rustproofed +6 Mjollnir).  I had blah armor and a cloak of magic resistance
donated by a deceased wizard.  I got gauntlets of power, identified all wands
and rings (and most gems), and got a -11 AC (not good, but it did well with
weapons).  Another adventurer donated gray dragon scale mail to top off the
collection.  Anyway, I've always been annoyed by elves and soldiers.  From
exploration mode, I knew that if I genocided myself, I'd come back to life.  
I had an amulet of lifesaving, so I decided to give it a go.  So I get this
list of things that got the axe, and it comes to me, and I die.  I come back to
life and the medallion crumbles.  Then it says, "Unfortunately, you are still
genocided."

By the way, I noticed that when I ate another elf, it said "You cannibal!
You will regret this", but I could munch on humans all I wanted.  Nice
touch.  That makes two games that I would've almost certainly won if not 
for a pesky scroll of genocide (the first was when I accidently polymorphed
the Amulet into an amulet of restful sleep -- I figured I should go in
style).  Genocide isn't for the inept.

